.TH GIT-RB 1
.SH NAME
git-rb \- fetch and rebase onto a remote target branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git rb
.RI [ target-branch ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git rb
fetches
.BI origin/ target-branch
and rebases the current branch onto it.
When
.I target-branch
is omitted, the remote default branch from
.B origin/HEAD
is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git rb
    Rebase onto the remote default branch.

git rb main
    Rebase onto origin/main.

git rb release/1.0
    Rebase onto origin/release/1.0.
.fi
